    "created_at": "2026-02-17T21:48:53.4875554Z",
    "response": " Let's denote the amount invested in the first account as \\( x \\) dollars. Since the total investment is $12,000, the amount invested in the second account will be \\( 12000 - x \\) dollars.\n\nThe interest rate for the first account is 4.2% compounded monthly, which means the monthly interest rate is \\( \\frac{4.2\\%}{12} = 0.35\\% = 0.0035 \\). The amount in the first account after 3 years (which is 36 months) can be calculated using the compound interest formula:\n\\[ A_1 = x \\left(1 + \\frac{0.042}{12}\\right)^{36} = x (1.0035)^{36} \\]\n\nThe interest rate for the second account is 6.0% compounded monthly, which means the monthly interest rate is \\( \\frac{6.0\\%}{12} = 0.5\\% = 0.005 \\). The amount in the second account after 3 years (which is 36 months) can be calculated using the compound interest formula:\n\\[ A_2 = (12000 - x) \\left(1 + \\frac{0.06}{12}\\right)^{36} = (12000 - x) (1.005)^{36} \\]\n\nAccording to the problem, the total amount after 3 years is $14,600. Therefore, we can set up the following equation:\n\\[ A_1 + A_2 = 14600 \\]\n\\[ x (1.0035)^{36} + (12000 - x) (1.005)^{36} = 14600 \\]\n\nFirst, we calculate \\( (1.0035)^{36} \\) and \\( (1.005)^{36} \\):\n\\[ (1.0035)^{36} \\approx 1.1359 \\]\n\\[ (1.005)^{36} \\approx 1.1967 \\]\n\nSubstituting these values into the equation, we get:\n\\[ x \\cdot 1.1359 + (12000 - x) \\cdot 1.1967 = 14600 \\]\n\\[ 1.1359x + 14360.4 - 1.1967x = 14600 \\]\n\\[ -0.0608x + 14360.4 = 14600 \\]\n\\[ -0.0608x = 14600 - 14360.4 \\]\n\\[ -0.0608x = 239.6 \\]\n\\[ x = \\frac{239.6}{-0.0608} \\]\n\\[ x = 3925 \\]\n\nSo, the amount invested in the first account is $3925. The amount invested in the second account is:\n\\[ 12000 - 3925 = 8075 \\]\n\nTherefore, the amounts put in each account are \\(\\boxed{3925 \\text{ and } 8075}\\).",
